[FIND] THE RLS LAYER IS THE BACKSTOP, NOT THE OPERATIVE GATE
       The application connects as `postgres`, which carries rolbypassrls, so in production the two policy assertions above do not fire on the app's own connection at all — the app-layer is_super_admin check and the service's _require_super_admin are what actually refuse an org admin. Both are asserted separately, through the real ASGI app. The policies are what catches a direct psql session or a future mis-roled pool.

